cense, which permits unrestricted use,                distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2008</copyright-year><related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="3" page="e3095" id="N0x1c7ec30N0x1d997f0" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="18769485" ext-link-type="pubmed"><article-title>Computational Modelling of Genome-Side Transcription Assembly Networks Using a Fluidics Analogy</article-title></related-article></article-meta></front><body><p>The fifth word of the title was misspelled. This also affect the article's citation. The correct title should be: Computational Modelling of Genome-Wide Transcription Assembly Networks Using a Fluidics Analogy. The corrected citation is: Azmy YY, Gupta A, Pugh BF (2008) Computational Modelling of Genome-Wide Transcription Assembly Networks Using a Fluidics Analogy. PLoS ONE 3(8): e3095. doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0003095</p></body></article>